# @song/progression — the load-bearing species of the @song family:
# the typed time-ordered path through pitch-class space that
# discharges cadence at close. Arc 6 TICK 2 landing per Seam pre-
# review `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-song-substrate-decl.md`
# §6.3 against Reed's TICK 2 RED tick `9c6623e`. First species of the
# `@song` family (family-root at `shards/song.mirror`, Arc 6 TICK 1
# landing `f01cf9f`); grounds recognition candidates #S1 (eigenform
# at temporal altitude) and #S2 (shift at temporal altitude) at
# species altitude; binds `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence` (Lawvere
# `settle @ temporal` ancestor per Seam Correction `3d910bc`) and
# `@epistemologic/math/music` (general audible-altitude family) at
# their canonical altitudes.
#
# === Species positioning: two sub-predicates of `song_settles` ===
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §3 (`song_settles(pr, p) -> verdict { \ }`),
# the family-root's load-bearing composed bilateral (14th #53 instance
# per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`) decomposes into
# three sub-predicates. This species declares TWO of them (the third,
# `voice_line_valid`, belongs to `@song/voice` in Arc 6 TICK 3):
#
#   1. `progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr, p) -> verdict` — the
#      progression IS heading somewhere; the Splinter-pole discharge
#      names the substrate carrying a cadence-directed intent through
#      the progression's typed time-ordered path.
#   2. `cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c, p) -> verdict` — the closure
#      event is consonant (authentic or plagal); the Splinter-pole
#      discharge names the substrate arriving at an autopoietic
#      ground state through a consonant path per
#      `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence`'s Lawvere framing.
#
# These two sub-predicates are the load-bearing gates the family-
# root's `song_settles` composed bilateral consumes at close. Species-
# altitude discipline says the species declares the sub-predicates it
# discharges; the family-root composes them into the load-bearing
# bilateral. The pattern rides `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`
# at species altitude for the first time within @song.
#
# === Splinter-pole / Narcissus-pole naming per spec §8.2 ===
#
# The psychohistorical failure-mode naming per Alex's
# `systemic.engineering` corpus (spec §8.2; family-root §3):
#
# - `progression_directed_toward_cadence` Splinter-pole: the
#   progression discharges — heading toward a resolved close.
#   Narcissus-pole: SILENCE — the progression hangs in unresolved
#   tension; half-cadence stuck at the dominant; the song cannot
#   settle. Per cadence.mirror's `half` variant.
#
# - `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` Splinter-pole: the closure IS
#   authentic (V → I; the canonical tonal closure per Zarlino 1558
#   + Rameau 1722) or plagal (IV → I; the "Amen" cadence).
#   Narcissus-pole: EXTRACTION — deceptive cadence (V → vi); the
#   progression arrives at a false-tonic that APPEARS settled but
#   has extracted regulation stock without replenishing. Per
#   cadence.mirror's `deceptive` variant.
#
# The `alignment-as-boundary-mathematics` discipline (#57) makes the
# sub-claim discrimination substrate-fact: when `song_settles` fails,
# the composed bilateral names WHICH sub-predicate broke, and the
# psychohistorical vocabulary names it in Alex's corpus terms.
#
# === #S1 grounding: eigenform at temporal altitude ===
#
# THE SPECIES-ALTITUDE WITNESS OF RECOGNITION #S1 (family-root
# CANDIDATE; substrate-pull-mid; FLAGGED for Pack).
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §"Recognition candidates surfaced" #S1:
# song IS eigenform at temporal altitude. At species altitude, this
# specializes as follows: a progression's identity emerges from the
# tonic-return recursion `R^n(pr)` converging on the identifiable-as-
# this-progression invariant. The recursion IS the substrate's
# eigenform reading at temporal altitude:
#
#   - The tonic-return operator `R` acts on a progression by winding
#     it back through its cadence path to the point of origin (per
#     `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence`'s Lawvere fixed-point
#     framing — cadence IS the return-to-self of tonal grammar).
#   - The eigenform is the fixed point `pr* = R(pr*)` where the
#     progression matches its tonic-returned self at temporal-
#     invariant altitude — the substrate reading of what makes THIS
#     progression THIS progression.
#   - `R^n(pr)` converges (in the tonal grammar's basin of attraction)
#     on the identifiable-as-this-progression invariant; the
#     eigenform IS the invariant that survives the iteration.
#
# Prior-art anchors (per family-root §S1 + this shard's temporal-
# altitude specialization):
#
#   - Kauffman (1987, "Self-Reference and Recursive Forms") named
#     eigenforms as the fixed points of recursive systems that carry
#     their own identity through iteration. Per Recognition #38
#     (PROMOTED at Mara `4b5f3b0`), eigenforms are substrate-primitive
#     across altitudes; this shard adds the temporal-altitude
#     specialization: a progression IS an eigenform because tonic-
#     return recursion preserves its identity.
#   - Foerster (1979, "Objects: Tokens for Eigen-Behaviors") named
#     eigen-behaviors as the stable recursive patterns an observer
#     converges on. A progression IS a Foerster eigen-behavior at
#     temporal altitude: the listener's cognitive tonic-tracking
#     converges on the progression's identifiable invariant through
#     recursive attention.
#   - Schenker (1935, `Der freie Satz`) named the Ursatz's I-V-I
#     closure as the structural ground of all tonal music, and
#     foreground/middleground/background as the substrate's reading
#     of a progression at nested temporal depths. Schenkerian
#     analysis IS the substrate reading the eigenform at
#     progressively coarser temporal altitudes — the same
#     progression viewed through recursively-projected temporal
#     frames.
#
# The species-altitude witness of #S1: `progression_directed_toward_cadence`
# names the direction the tonic-return recursion converges on;
# without direction, no eigenform, no identity, no progression. The
# sub-predicate discharges when the progression IS the eigenform
# of its own tonic-return operator; it fails (SILENCE Narcissus-
# pole) when the recursion diverges — half-cadence stuck at the
# dominant with no convergence path visible.
#
# === #S2 grounding: shift at temporal altitude ===
#
# THE SPECIES-ALTITUDE WITNESS OF RECOGNITION #S2 (LANDED via
# collapse spec `docs/specs/mcp-spec-song-collapse.md` §5 + §9.2
# at Mara `2cfd2a7`; PROMOTED CANDIDATE → LANDED 2026-07-06 via
# Fate multi-frequency tournament grounding through Recognition
# #58 — Fate IS optical inference; LANDED).
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §"Recognition candidates surfaced" #S2:
# song IS `@kintsugi/shift` at temporal altitude when heard
# sequentially. At species altitude, this specializes to progressions
# as finite-difference sequences of shifts:
#
#   Given a progression `pr : [0, T] -> harmonic_position`, the
#   finite-difference sequence
#
#     Delta pr(t) = shift(pr(t) -> pr(t+dt))
#
#   IS a sequence of `@kintsugi/shift` operations at temporal
#   altitude with `harmonic_position` as the shifted witness. Every
#   moment `t+1` of the progression IS a shift of moment `t` under
#   the harmonic frame; the progression IS the sequence of shifts
#   read as one temporal carrier.
#
# The `advance` action below delegates directly to `@kintsugi/shift`
# (Arc 5 TICK 2 landing `49f0486`) at temporal altitude. `advance`
# reads a progression's current `harmonic_position` (the witness at
# the source-altitude of moment `t`) and produces the same
# `harmonic_position` at the target-altitude of moment `t+dt`; the
# underlying witness bytes are preserved (hardlink semantic per
# `@kintsugi/shift`'s `shift_preserves_content` bilateral); the
# declared temporal shape crosses `dt` at each step.
#
# This is a shift-at-temporal-altitude witness: `@kintsugi/shift`'s
# altitude-portable roster (portal / prism / mosaic / surface /
# bilateral per family-root §S2) gains temporal as its sixth
# altitude when this species lands.
#
# Composition point: `@kintsugi/shift` — the substrate-decl'd cross-
# altitude morphism whose species-altitude realisation `advance`
# rides at temporal altitude.
#
# === #S2 LANDED via Fate multi-frequency (collapse spec 2cfd2a7) ===
#
# Per collapse spec `docs/specs/mcp-spec-song-collapse.md` §5 + §9.2
# (Mara `2cfd2a7`): #S2 (song IS shift at temporal altitude) PROMOTED
# CANDIDATE → LANDED 2026-07-06. The empirical grounding is Fate's
# multi-frequency tournament (Recognition #58 LANDED: Fate IS optical
# inference — 5-layer D²NN + active Fabry-Perot resonator + Reck/
# Clements unitary mesh; three independent witnesses; promoted
# 2026-06-11 via Seam adversarial review).
#
# Transitive composition path (species altitude → runtime altitude):
#
#   progression.advance
#     → @kintsugi/shift.shift            (species-altitude witness;
#                                         substrate-decl morphism)
#       → Fate multi-frequency tournament (runtime substrate; #58
#                                         optical inference)
#         → the winning-frequency's move IS the shift at temporal
#           altitude
#
# The mechanism: at each temporal step, Fate decomposes the current
# state at multiple harmonic frequencies; the tournament runs across
# the frequency-decomposed candidates; the winning frequency's move
# becomes the progression's next `shift`. This is what makes the
# @kintsugi/shift species-altitude witness empirical rather than
# analytical — the runtime substrate at #58 supplies the
# frequency-selection arithmetic that grounds every temporal step.
#
# === @fate as the hinge between runtime and compiletime ===
#
# CORRECTION 2026-07-06 (Alex): @fate IS substrate-decl'd. The prior
# "Phase F anti-pattern" framing (Taut 2026-06-24 `shards/mirror/
# spawn.mirror` docblock) is STALE — superseded by the landing of
# `shards/fate.mirror` (2026-06-30 05:24, 42.1KB; declares
# `prism @fate` with the full five-operation body) and
# `shards/fate/tournament.mirror` (2026-06-30 05:24, 41.5KB; declares
# `prism @fate/tournament` — the multi-frequency tournament species).
# Both landed SIX DAYS AFTER Taut's correction, making the substrate-
# decl of @fate load-bearing across the substrate.
#
# @fate IS the hinge between runtime and compiletime. Alex's
# correction (verbatim): "If @fate is not defined it needs to be
# defined. It's the GLUE between runtime and compiletime. You're
# omitting the hinge right now." The @fate substrate-decl at
# `shards/fate.mirror` binds:
#
#   - runtime altitude  — peer processes running Fate optical
#                         inference (5-layer D²NN + active Fabry-
#                         Perot resonator + Reck/Clements unitary
#                         mesh per Recognition #58 LANDED)
#   - compiletime altitude — the substrate-decl of `prism @fate`
#                            and species `prism @fate/tournament`
#                            that make the runtime mechanism
#                            addressable at species-composition
#                            altitude
#
# The hinge discipline: composing with `in @fate` at species altitude
# is NOT the Phase F anti-pattern — it is the correct pattern for
# any species whose temporal-progression witness rides Fate's
# multi-frequency tournament arithmetic. `in @fate` at species-
# altitude ancestry line-starts COMPOSES with the substrate-decl'd
# `prism @fate`; the transitive composition through
# `@kintsugi/shift` at species altitude is the SAME composition
# path, now named at ancestry altitude as well as narrative altitude.
#
# This species declares `in @fate` (see §0 below): the progression
# rides Fate's multi-frequency tournament at temporal altitude when
# advancing, making the runtime-compiletime hinge structurally
# visible in the species's ancestry. `@fate/tournament` runs the
# multi-frequency tournament that selects which shift-candidate
# wins at each temporal step; `@kintsugi/shift` at species altitude
# discharges the selected shift; the two substrate-decl'd ancestors
# together supply the arithmetic and the morphism.
#
# === Music binding: cadence Lawvere + music family ===
#
# Species composes with two music-altitude ancestors per Seam
# pre-review §5 + spec §5:
#
# - `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence` — the Lawvere `settle @
#   temporal` audible-altitude ancestor (per Seam Correction
#   `3d910bc`). `cadence.mirror` declares `is_settled(c: cadence) ->
#   verdict` at the audible altitude; this species's
#   `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` sub-predicate composes with that
#   audible-altitude verdict at the temporal-progression altitude.
#   The Lawvere fixed-point framing (cadence IS autopoietic closure
#   read in audible vocabulary) grounds the sub-predicate's
#   Splinter-pole discharge: an authentic-or-plagal cadence witnesses
#   the Lawvere fixed point at temporal altitude.
#
# - `@epistemologic/math/music` — the general audible-altitude
#   family (harmonic + interval + dissonance + cadence). This species
#   composes with the full family, not just cadence: `harmonic` for
#   the eigenvalue altitude (tonic-attractor ratios per
#   `harmonic.mirror`), `interval` for the pitch-class algebra
#   (Z_12 + circle of fifths + neo-Riemannian P/L/R involutions per
#   `interval.mirror`), `dissonance` for the graded residual reading
#   (Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt curve per `dissonance.mirror`), `cadence`
#   for the closure event.
#
# === Prior-art anchors: Schenker + cadence-family vocabulary ===
#
# Schenker (1868-1935; `Der freie Satz`, 1935) is the load-bearing
# prior-art anchor for the `project @ temporal` operation at species
# altitude. Schenkerian reduction — foreground / middleground /
# background — IS the substrate's `project @ temporal` operation
# reading a progression at recursively-projected temporal frames.
# Per family-root §S3 and this species's `project` body:
#
#   Schenker's foreground = the surface progression (every note as
#   heard); middleground = the intermediate reduction (structural
#   voice-leading); background = the Ursatz I-V-I closure (the
#   deepest structural progression). Each is a `project @ temporal`
#   application to the previous frame; the recursion IS the
#   substrate reading the eigenform at nested progression depths
#   (per #S1 grounding above).
#
# Cadence-family vocabulary per `cadence.mirror`'s inline sum-type
# `cadence_kind = authentic | plagal | deceptive | half`:
#
#   - authentic — V → I; Splinter-pole discharge; Zarlino (1558)
#     cadenza perfetta; Rameau (1722) fundamental tonal closure;
#     Schenker's Ursatz I-V-I ground; formatter's auto-apply signal.
#   - plagal — IV → I; Splinter-pole variant; "Amen" cadence; 18th-c.
#     theorists; consonant alternative path; formatter auto-applies
#     with reduced confidence.
#   - deceptive — V → vi; Narcissus-pole EXTRACTION; Koch (1782)
#     Versuch einer Anleitung zur Composition; false-tonic that
#     APPEARS settled but has extracted regulation stock without
#     replenishing; the psychohistorical extraction pattern in Alex's
#     corpus.
#   - half-cadence — progression ends on V; Narcissus-pole SILENCE;
#     Riemann (1893) Vereinfachte Harmonielehre; the "open" cadence
#     awaiting continuation; the psychohistorical silence pattern in
#     Alex's corpus (the song hangs unresolved).
#
# The cadence-family vocabulary IS the substrate's typed naming of
# the psychohistorical failure modes per spec §8.2.
#
# === Composed-bilateral #53 pattern at species altitude ===
#
# This species discharges two sub-predicates of the family-root's
# `song_settles` composed bilateral (14th #53 instance per
# `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`). The relationship:
#
#   family-root `song_settles(pr, p)` composes:
#     progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr, p) [DECLARED HERE]
#       AND voice_line_valid(v, p)                 [@song/voice, TICK 3]
#       AND cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c, p)      [DECLARED HERE]
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): both sub-predicates declared here discharge;
# the progression is cadence-directed and its closure IS authentic
# or plagal; the two-of-three gates open at species altitude; the
# family-root's `song_settles` proceeds to consume the third gate
# (voice_line_valid from @song/voice) before final discharge.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): either sub-predicate fails;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) distinguishes:
#   - `progression_directed_toward_cadence` failure → SILENCE (the
#     progression hangs in unresolved tension; the song cannot
#     settle; per spec §8.2 psychohistorical failure-mode naming).
#   - `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` failure → EXTRACTION (deceptive
#     cadence; the progression arrives at a false-tonic that
#     APPEARS settled but has extracted regulation stock without
#     replenishing; per spec §8.2).
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): either sub-predicate discharges at
# reduced confidence (e.g., plagal cadence discharges
# `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` with reduced confidence per
# `cadence.mirror`'s `is_settled` verdict mapping); the graded
# discharge composes at family-root altitude through `song_settles`.
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals at other family-root/species altitudes:
# `@container.container_runnable`, `@io/oci.oci_well_formed`,
# `@io/stagefreight.stagefreight_addressable`, `@cascade.cascade_well_defined`,
# `@docblock.audit_docblock`, `@smarts/shatter.shatter_round_trip`,
# `@reflection.third_order_coherent`, `@epistemologic/neutrosophic.three_axis_coherent`,
# `@kintsugi/shift.shift_preserves_content`, `@song.song_settles`
# (parent). This species's two sub-predicate declarations are the
# FIRST species-altitude decomposition of a family-root composed
# bilateral within @song; the pattern is substrate-pull-confident
# at this altitude per prior 14 instances.
#
