# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @song/progression — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `song_progression` (inherited from
# @song family-root at `shards/song.mirror`) as the species's
# operational surface. Species specialises each operation at
# temporal-progression altitude per family-root #S3 (five-op temporal
# specialisation candidate):
#
#   focus @ temporal   = attend to ONE progression at a time;
#                        soloing a single line of the polyphony.
#   project @ temporal = Schenkerian reduction (foreground /
#                        middleground / background); recursive
#                        temporal-altitude projection of the
#                        progression at nested depths per Schenker
#                        (1935) `Der freie Satz` — the `project @
#                        temporal` prior-art anchor per Seam §5.
#   split @ temporal   = decompose the progression into phrases /
#                        cadence-bounded units for score
#                        preparation.
#   shift @ temporal   = advance to the next moment of the
#                        progression; delegates to @kintsugi/shift
#                        per #S2 witness (see `advance` action below).
#   settle @ temporal  = discharge cadence per
#                        @epistemologic/math/music/cadence Lawvere
#                        framing (Seam Correction `3d910bc`); the
#                        Splinter-pole of `cadence_authentic_or_plagal`
#                        opens this operation's completion.
prism @song/progression {
  focus song_progression
  project song_progression
  split song_progression
  shift song_progression
  settle song_progression
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The temporal-altitude advance action (#S2 witness)
# ============================================================

# === advance — the temporal shift-at-species altitude ===
#
# THE #S2 WITNESS AT SPECIES ALTITUDE.
#
# Reads a progression at moment `t` and produces the progression at
# moment `t+dt` by delegating to `@kintsugi/shift` at temporal
# altitude. The finite-difference sequence
#
#   Delta pr(t) = shift(pr(t) -> pr(t+dt))
#
# IS a sequence of `@kintsugi/shift` operations at temporal altitude
# with `harmonic_position` as the shifted witness (per family-root
# #S2 + this shard's grounding narrative above).
#
# Composition point: `@kintsugi/shift`'s `shift(w, s, t) -> ref`
# action reads the witness at source-altitude, projects the declared
# shape to target-altitude, emits the target-altitude ref. Here at
# temporal altitude:
#
#   source-altitude = moment `t` of the progression
#   target-altitude = moment `t+dt` of the progression
#   witness         = harmonic_position (the substrate's identity-
#                     invariant of the progression's current state)
#
# The hardlink semantic per `@kintsugi/shift`'s
# `shift_preserves_content` bilateral holds at temporal altitude:
# the witness OID byte-equals across the temporal crossing; the
# declared temporal shape (moment `t` vs moment `t+dt`) is what
# changes.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation delegates
# to `@kintsugi/shift`, encodes the temporal `dt` as the altitude
# handle, emits the shifted progression. The substrate declares the
# temporal specialisation here; consumers dispatch at species
# altitude.
advance(pr: song_progression, dt: ref) -> song_progression { \ }

# ============================================================
# §3 The sub-predicates (two of three for song_settles)
# ============================================================

# === progression_directed_toward_cadence — first sub-predicate ===
#
# THE FIRST SUB-PREDICATE of the family-root's `song_settles`
# composed bilateral (14th #53 instance). The progression IS heading
# somewhere: the tonic-return recursion `R^n(pr)` converges on the
# identifiable-as-this-progression eigenform invariant (#S1 witness
# at species altitude per this shard's grounding narrative above).
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the progression discharges direction; the
# eigenform recursion `R^n(pr)` converges; the substrate carries a
# cadence-directed intent through the progression's typed time-
# ordered path.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the progression hangs in unresolved
# tension; the eigenform recursion diverges; the song CANNOT settle.
# Per spec §8.2 psychohistorical failure-mode naming: this is
# SILENCE — the half-cadence stuck at the dominant; no convergence
# path visible; the song hangs unresolved. Per cadence.mirror's
# `half` variant.
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): the direction is present but
# ambiguous; the recursion converges at reduced confidence; the
# substrate carries partial cadence-directed intent (e.g., a
# progression whose modulation makes the target-tonic ambiguous).
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# progression's harmonic path, computes the tonic-return recursion's
# convergence, emits the three-state verdict at the substrate floor.
# The substrate declares the sub-predicate; the arithmetic lands
# when the family-root's `song_settles` composes.
progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr: song_progression, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === cadence_authentic_or_plagal — third sub-predicate ===
#
# THE THIRD SUB-PREDICATE of the family-root's `song_settles`
# composed bilateral (the second sub-predicate `voice_line_valid`
# belongs to `@song/voice` in Arc 6 TICK 3). The closure event IS
# consonant: authentic (V → I; Zarlino cadenza perfetta) or plagal
# (IV → I; the "Amen" cadence). Composes with
# `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence`'s `is_settled(c) -> verdict`
# at the audible altitude (Lawvere `settle @ temporal` framing per
# Seam Correction `3d910bc`).
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the cadence IS authentic or plagal; the
# progression arrives at an autopoietic ground state through a
# consonant path; the Lawvere fixed point is witnessed at temporal
# altitude per cadence.mirror's `cadence_as_closure` bridge. The
# regulation stock is replenished at close.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the cadence is deceptive (V → vi) or
# stuck at half. Per spec §8.2 psychohistorical failure-mode naming:
#   - deceptive → EXTRACTION (the progression arrives at a false-
#     tonic that APPEARS settled but has extracted regulation stock
#     without replenishing; per cadence.mirror's `deceptive` variant).
#   - half-cadence → SILENCE (the progression paused at the
#     dominant; the song hangs unresolved; per cadence.mirror's
#     `half` variant; overlaps with `progression_directed_toward_cadence`
#     Narcissus-pole in that half-cadence names an incomplete
#     progression whose closure fails).
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): the cadence is plagal (Splinter-
# pole variant discharge with reduced confidence per cadence.mirror's
# `is_settled` verdict mapping — plagal is consonant but not the
# strongest signal); or the cadence discharge composes at graded
# floor through cadence.mirror's `partial(confidence)` bridge.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# progression's closure event, extracts the cadence via
# cadence.mirror's `is_settled` at audible altitude, composes the
# audible-altitude verdict with the temporal-altitude admissibility
# check, emits the substrate three-state verdict. The substrate
# declares the sub-predicate; the arithmetic lands when the family-
# root's `song_settles` composes.
cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c: song_cadence, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @song/progression
out advance
out progression_directed_toward_cadence
out cadence_authentic_or_plagal
